#Frequently asked questions (Home Office)


##Access & Onboarding 

**When should I start using the EMO service?** 

From 2 July 2026, all Home Office users will be onboarded. 

**Do I need to use the EMO service even if I’m busy with other initiatives?**

Yes. The service is mandatory from your onboarding date. Support is available via Microsoft Teams and the weekly drop-ins. 


##Order Submission Guidance 

**How do I know if an order has been accepted?**

You will receive a successful submission message on the service when you have successfully submitted an order. This will act as a receipt that your order has been sent to the installer, and you will not receive email confirmation. However, you will not receive confirmation from the installer if an order has been successfully processed. You will hear from the installer  if an order has been rejected or requires more information, where you will then be instructed on what to do in order to resubmit an order.  


##Attachments 

**Can I attach documentation such as photos and exclusion zone maps?** 

Yes. Exclusion zone maps can be attached in the relevant field is ‘Exclusion Zone Monitoring’ is selected on the Electronic Monitoring requirements page.  

You can also attach a copy of the device wearer's photo in the ‘Additional documents’ page. You should not submit an order without a photo.


##Search and change 

**Can I search submitted forms and reuse data for changes?**

Yes, you can search forms that have been submitted by you and other individuals in your cohort. To find these submissions, click the ‘Submitted forms’ tab on your dashboard and search for the device wearer. You can search by device wearer’s first name and/or last name or personal identity number entered on the original order. For example, their CEPR number.  

**Can I edit submitted orders and amend individual fields?** 

Yes, you can change orders that have been submitted by searching for them, viewing them and clicking the 'Make changes to this form' button.

**Will future updates auto-fill prisoner info from Atlas?**

This is being explored but not expected soon. Updates will be communicated. 


## What can't I do in the service yet?

**How do I request a visit for refits or equipment checks?**

Use the service request portal.

**How do I send a 'Special' order for a high-risk device wearer?**

- complete the 'EMS NSD CPPC SOC order form' 
- send the completed form by email to emCCSpecialCase@ems.co.uk


## Orders not created in EMO

EMO does not have a record of orders created by email. 

**How do I change an order that was not created in EMO? For example, change an address or change from a fitted to non fitted device.**

To change a form that was not created in EMO search for the form and click the 'Tell us about changes to form a sent by email' link in the no results found message. 

You will have to enter all the information again so there are a couple of exceptions below where you can use email.

**How do I change the telephone number for an order that was not created in EMO?**

Use the Bail 206 form and email it to [HOIEorders@ems.co.uk](HOIEorders@ems.co.uk).

**How do I end an order that was not created in EMO?**

Use the Bail 206 form and email it to [HOIEorders@ems.co.uk](HOIEorders@ems.co.uk)


## 'Cease and new'

**How do I 'cease and new' an order in EMO?**

In EMO, this will be done as two separate actions: first end the existing order, then create a new order.​

There are plans to introduce a ‘clone order’ feature in future to make this quicker and easier.


##Rejections and what to do next?  

Rejections of orders are to be expected, as often there are mistakes made or information missing that is required to process the order. Below are the types of rejections commonly experienced by users on the new service, information on what to do to avoid rejections, and what to do if you have a rejection.  

**Submitting a change to an order after a rejection**

If you have an order rejected, you should:

- Go into the EMO service and search for your order by device wearer’s first name and/or last name or personal identity number entered on the original order

- Follow the steps to make a change to the order

- Select 'Yes' to the question 'Are you making changes to this form because the original was rejected by email?' 

- Rectify the issues as stated in the email and submit -  - this is now quicker and easier to do, and you can edit the fields you need without needing to start a blank form 

**Photo attachments**

It is mandatory to attach a photo of the device wearer, and the order will be rejected without a photo. 


 
